"Embeddium - Minecraft Mod (https://modrinth.com/mod/embeddium)\nciteturn19view0 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://modrinth.com/mod/embeddium\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 122\nL0: ?\nL1: \nL2: Discover cite0†Host a server cite1†Modrinth App L3: \nL4: cite2†Sign in L5: \nL6: cite3†Mods cite4†Resource Packs cite5†Data Packs cite6†Shaders cite7†Modpacks cite8†Plugins cite9†Servers L7: \nL8: cite2†Sign in L9: \nL10: cite10†Settings Change theme\nL11: \nL12: cite11†Image: Embeddium†cdn.modrinth.com L13: \nL14: # Embeddium\nL15: \nL16: A powerful, mod-friendly, FOSS client performance mod for NeoForge\nL17: \nL18: 37.1M downloads\nL19: \nL20: 2K followers\nL21: \nL22: 37.1M downloads\nL23: \nL24: 2K followers\nL25: \nL26: ## Compatibility\nL27: \nL28: ### Minecraft: Java Edition\nL29: \nL30: 1.21.4\nL31: \nL32: 1.21–1.21.1\nL33: \nL34: 1.20.1–1.20.6\nL35: \nL36: 1.19.2\nL37: \nL38: 1.18.2\nL39: \nL40: 1.16.5\nL41: ### Platforms\nL42: \nL43: Fabric Forge NeoForge\nL44: \nL45: ### Supported environments\nL46: \nL47: Client-side\nL48: \nL49: ## Links\nL50: \nL51: cite12†Report issues†github.com cite13†View source†github.com L52: \nL53: * * *\nL54: \nL55: cite14†Donate on Ko-fi†ko-fi.com L56: \nL57: ## Tags\nL58: \nL59: Optimization\nL60: \nL61: ## Creators\nL62: \nL63: ## Details\nL64: \nL65: Licensed LGPL-3.0-only\nL66: \nL67: Published 3 years ago\nL68: \nL69: Updated 2 years ago\nL70: \nL71: cite15†Description cite16†Gallery cite17†Changelog cite18†Versions L72: # Embeddium\nL73: \nL74: Embeddium is a free and open-source performance mod for Minecraft clients. It is based on the last FOSS-licensed version of the Sodium codebase, and includes additional bugfixes & features for better mod compatibility.\nL75: \nL76: Despite being forked from Sodium, Embeddium is not supported by CaffeineMC. Do not report issues encountered with it to their bug tracker or in their Discord.\nL77: ## Highlights\nL78:   * All performance improvements from Sodium 0.5.8 and earlier, i.e. a rewritten terrain renderer, various optimizations to the immediate-mode rendering pipeline (used by entities, GUIs, block entities, etc.), and other miscellaneous improvements\nL79:   * Available for Minecraft Forge on 1.20.1 and older, Fabric on 1.20.1-1.20.6, and NeoForge on 1.20.1 and newer\nL80:   * Integrated Fabric Rendering API support (Indium is no longer required, and will not work with Embeddium)\nL81:   * Frequent patch updates to fix mod compatibility issues soon after being reported & reproduced\nL82:   * Additional APIs for mod integration\nL83:   * Optional support for translucency sorting (can be enabled in Video Settings)\nL84: ## For developers\nL85: \nL86: If you're looking to add Embeddium to your development environment, please take a look at the cite19†dedicated wiki page†github.com for instructions & recommended guidelines for integration.\nL87: ## Credits\nL88: \nL89:   * JellySquid & the CaffeineMC team, for making Sodium in the first place, without which this project would not be possible\nL90:   * Asek3, for the initial port to Forge\nL91:   * XFactHD, for providing a list of gamebreaking Rubidium issues to start this work off, and for testing early builds\nL92:   * Pepper, for their invaluable assistance with getting Forge lighting to work on Sodium 0.5\nL93:   * @CelestialAbyss and @input-Here for making the new logo design\nL94: ## License\nL95: \nL96: Embeddium is distributed under the Lesser GNU General Public License version 3. For more details, refer to our cite13†GitHub†github.com repository.\nL97: \nL98: ## Need a Minecraft server? Consider CreeperHost!\nL99: \nL100: cite20†Image: Use code taumc-qk0 for 10% off†cdn.modrinth.com L101: \nL102: Modrinth is cite21†open source†github.com .\nL103: \nL104: © 2026 Rinth, Inc.\nL105: \nL106: ### About\nL107: \nL108: cite22†News cite23†Changelog cite24†S